+*   **Memory Complexity**: The in-memory representation is proportional to the number of non-background nodes and tiles [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Performance**: Reading is generally fast due to the compact binary format and efficient compression [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Strengths**: Efficient storage of sparse data, fast random access to nodes after loading, support for various data types and compression methods [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations**: Multi-buffer trees are not supported. Half-float handling may be implementation-specific. Blosc decompression fails if the uncompressed size is 0 [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-OpenVDB is an open-source C++ library developed by DreamWorks Animation for the storage and manipulation of large volumetric datasets, particularly for visual effects. The file format is designed to be compact and efficient for sparse data. The parsing method described here is based on the implementation details found in the `woxel` library [S1, unofficial].
